From 266882ee79104153a1093b3fdc356cae2cc507e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:33:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] wip/kv-residency A13: the fused indexer scorer accepts
 QUANTIZED keys (q8_0 and the q4/q5 family)

The fused INDEXER_SCORE + derived INDEXER_FILL path (both default-on) served only F32/BF16/F16 indexer keys, so a
quantized KV cache -- the delivery's large-context type, and the one block 15's windowed KV takes by construction
-- fell back to the per-op chain: get_rows(dequantize) -> pool copy -> scale -> rms_norm -> rope_multi -> score
mat_mul -> relu -> head-sum -> bias add, re-materialising the WHOLE indexer key cache in F32 every step (47 MiB at
103k; measured at 5.31 ms/token of generic ops plus the 1.83 ms copy A12 fixed).

This teaches the two kernels a quantized key-row load: 32-element blocks whose byte size is nb[0], dequantized by
ggml's OWN helpers (dequantize_q8_0/q4_0/q4_1/q5_0/q5_1/q4_nl) -- i.e. the same values get_rows produces, which is
what keeps the paths byte-identical.  Note the two packings: q8_0 holds one element per byte, the 4/5-bit types put
a byte's low nibble at channel b and its high nibble at b+16.

  * indexer-score.cu: indexer_score_ld_chan(row, c, nb0K, ktype) replaces indexer_score_ld_val(element addr); the
    pooling helper is now row-addressed (a bit-identical address for the float types, where nb0K == 4/2/2).
    indexer_score_ktype() maps the type to the kernel code (0..8, -1 unsupported) and both _supported predicates
    and both impls' asserts use it.
  * ggml_indexer_key_type_supported() (ggml.h/ggml.c): one predicate for the constructors, the CUDA kernels and the
    memory layer; the two indexer ctors accept the widened set.
  * qwen4exp.cpp: idx_key_float -> idx_key_fused (the predicate), so a quantized cache takes the fused path.
  * llama-memory-hybrid-idx.cpp: pool_create builds the derived pool for those types too.

Gates (Flash-Next IQ3_XXS, 1 GPU, -ncmoe 48, PLE flags, ROCBLAS_USE_HIPBLASLT=0; the A/B arm is the pre-change
per-op chain, GGML_CUDA_QSA_INDEXER_SCORE=0):

  text, 5.3k, greedy -- identical on EVERY supported key type (fused vs chain): q8_0 296 91ef8940d66e /
  sparse 332 dd1981213373 (both == the pre-change build's hashes), f16 333 c42a586a6d13, bf16 296 91ef8940d66e,
  q4_0 307 097ff06194d6, q4_1 307 097ff06194d6, q5_0 336 bd82b7ed544c, q5_1 296 3205db133b1d, iq4_nl 323
  d7aba1c58e0c.  q8_0 with GGML_CUDA_QSA_INDEXER_CACHE=0 (fused, no derived pool) also matches.
  text, 51 475 depth, pool arm: q8_0 854 43b30de151b9 (== the pre-change hash); q4_0 841 65097e7c8630 fused ==
  chain.
  prefill-logit gate with --ub 1 (the decode graph, base arm = the chain): 0.000000 KLD / 100.000 % top-p.  The
  standard ctx-16384 gate against the A12 base: 0.000000 / 100.000 %.  test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_QSA OK.
  No GPU faults.

Worth (103k, arms interleaved):
  plain decode (the non-MTP path): 23.68 -> 17.73 ms/token of GPU kernel time, wall 29.3 -> 36.3 t/s (+24 %);
  the indexer bucket 5.31 -> 2.01 and "derived indexer cache (pool) = 12 layers ... ENABLED" for q8_0 (it said
  "skipped (q8_0 keys)" before).  That equals the bf16/fused arm's 17.83 ms/token and 36.2 t/s, i.e. the
  dequantizing kernel now delivers the whole fused-path prize on the product KV type.
  MTP-4 (-n 512): sparse 54.26 -> 54.70, pool 54.52 -> 54.65, dense unchanged at 59.10 -- small, because under MTP
  the indexer is amortised over ~2.84 tokens/step and the MoE/expert traffic dominates the token.
